  "resultText": "`GET /reports/no-shows?from=...&to=...` now works, and `npm test` passes: 31 unit tests and 6 e2e tests. Typecheck and lint are clean too.\n\n**Response:** for each practitioner with at least one no-show in the period, you get `{ practitionerId, noShows, totalFeesCents }`, sorted by practitioner. Practitioners with no no-shows in the period are left out.\n\n**Design:** no single context has both the practitioner (scheduling) and the fee (billing), and the contexts only talk through events. So I added a `reporting` module with its own table, `ReportingNoShow`, fed by two events:\n- **No-show:** `AppointmentNoShow` now also carries `practitionerId`. That is an additive change to the contract.\n- **Fee:** billing now publishes a new `billing.no-show-fee-charged` event, defined in `src/contracts/billing.events.ts`, after it issues a no-show invoice. `InvoicingService` therefore takes an `EventEmitter2`, and I updated its spec.\n- **Order and repeats:** the two events can arrive in either order, and each side updates only its own columns. A repeated event doesn't double-count.\n\n**Behaviours to be aware of:**\n- **Period:** it is `from` inclusive and `to` exclusive, matched against the appointment's start time.\n- **Validation:** a missing or unparseable `from` or `to` returns 400. A `from` that isn't before `to` returns 422 (`InvalidReportPeriodError`).\n- **Existing data:** only no-shows that happen after this deploys are reported. Nothing is backfilled from existing appointments or invoices.\n- **Schema:** the new table needs `npm run db:push`, and `npx prisma generate` for the client.\n\nI covered it with a service spec, an invoicing spec for the new event, and two e2e tests. One e2e test mixes practitioners, an out-of-period no-show and a cancelled appointment. The other covers period validation.",
